fy HOW the live-replay judges 'attributable to the new language' for post-fix cases — either a per-finding attribution protocol (e.g. inspect finding text/evidence for the fail-open/producer-liveness language) or design each post-fix no-fire diff so ANY finding is a genuine misfire — since code_review_no_fire only checks findings-presence and cannot express attribution.","cohort":["T8"],"criteria":["T8"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0778,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'a post-fix case none attributable to the new language' (Testing) and AC: 'all 9 post-fix cases are silent in the live replay'","code_review_no_fire is a presence-based scorer: REGISTRY maps it to _no_fire (src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_scorers.py:410), which for expect:pass simply checks the findings list is empty — it has no notion of 'attributable to the new language'","run_case (src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py:281) returns structured output scored by these presence-based scorers; no attribution mechanism exists","The tests overlay carries many other antipatterns (change-detector, under-mocking, non-gating) and the base reviewer covers correctness/error-handling broadly — a post-fix diff can legitimately fire a finding for a reason OTHER than the new fail-open language, which the 'silent' criterion cannot distinguish"],"finding":"The live-calibration step (and AC line 'all 9 post-fix cases are silent') relies on the decision rule 'a post-fix case [yields] none attributable to the new language', but the referenced scoring instrument (code_review_no_fire) scores only on findings PRESENCE/absence for expect:pass cases and cannot express attribution; the plan defines no protocol or fallback for a post-fix case that fires an UNRELATED finding on a live LLM replay.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa5bbacb6b9809ac3","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing §'Live calibration replay' + Acceptance Criteria (post-fix 'silent' AC)","norm_id":"n458b170044aec648","priority":0.7778,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A post-fix no-fire diff for instances 1-4 or 5-9 produces a finding on a pre-existing antipattern (e.g. under-mocking) unrelated to fail-open; the presence-based scorer marks it a false-fire even though the new language did not misfire","The calibration reviewer cannot decide whether a fired post-fix case disproves the new language or merely surfaced an incidental defect, blocking the 'escalate to a new criterion only if the language cannot fire from within these hosts' ruling"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Define the attribution rule in the Testing section: for each post-fix case, either (a) require the diff be otherwise clean so any finding is a real regression, or (b) hand-classify each fired finding by whether its evidence/finding text invokes the new producer-liveness/fail-open language, and record only new-language-attributable fires as failures. State the fallback: a post-fix finding NOT attributable to the new language does not fail calibration but must be noted in the ticket comment.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing"